      "side": 1,
      "message": "Design question.\n\nThe response exposes only a coarse hierarchy `version` — no per-definition fingerprint, no surviving-default, and no revision SHA — and the endpoint is project-scoped rather than revision-scoped.\n\nThis looks deliberate (the client owns built-ins and default selection, and the change already carries the revision SHA). Is that the intended contract for v1, to be revisited when path applicability lands and revision-scoped discovery becomes useful?\n\nNoting it so the divergence from the longer proposal is a conscious decision rather than an oversight.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "f43edcdd80bb08499cc4f1721a9cc6d4b6fc8108",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
