      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T08:51:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this is deliberate for v1: actions live in refs/meta/config, which doesn\u0027t vary by revision, and a revision-scoped URL would resolve and download all prompts again on every change open. The version covers every config revision in the hierarchy plus the plugin build, and before sending, the client compares the action\u0027s label and prompt with the current definition, so no per-action fingerprint is needed. v2 path matching is planned in the client against the revision\u0027s files, so the endpoint can stay project-scoped and just return `paths`.",
